C++20 brace initialization of std::vector with initializer_list
fails with 'struct nil is still incomplete'. This is a pre-existing
CBMC limitation affecting both libc++-18 and libc++-20.
Tagged KNOWNBUG 2026-07-23 (first full libc++ suite run):
C++20 concepts: substitution failure inside a concept-id's argument
must yield an unsatisfied constraint ([temp.constr.atomic]/3), not a
hard 'no match for same_as'; minimal WRONG-CODE root KNOWNBUG
cpp20_constraint_substitution_failure.  cpp20_ranges_basic
additionally aborts a unary-operand invariant (std_expr.h:380).
Update 2026-07-24: past the same_as front-end failure
([temp.constr.atomic]/3 atom classification); residual: semantic FAILUREs.
The same_as front-end failure is the requires-clause concept-template-id
parse gap, captured minimally in
cpp20_requires_clause_concept_template_id.
Update 2026-07-28: same vector-internal-pointer family as
cpp20_vector_basic_libcxx (see its note); header-free reduction
blocked on the typecheck_method_application crash.
Masking crash isolated: cpp20_extern_template_copy_ctor_abort.
